▶️ Run the application

Using Maven
mvn spring-boot:run

🧪 Run tests
mvn test

📡 API testing examples

📌 Quote Service API Documentation

This document describes the available REST API endpoints for the Quote Service backend built with Spring Boot.

Base URL:

http://localhost:8080/api/quotes
1. ➕ Create a Quote

Creates a new insurance quote.

Request
Invoke-WebRequest -Uri "http://localhost:8080/api/quotes" `
-Method POST `
-ContentType "application/json" `
-Body '{"productId": 1, "zoneCode": "TUN", "clientName": "John Doe", "clientAge": 30}'
2. 🔍 Get Quote by ID

Retrieves a specific quote using its ID.

Request
Invoke-WebRequest -Uri "http://localhost:8080/api/quotes/1" -Method GET
3. ➕ Create Another Quote

Example of creating a second quote.

Request
Invoke-WebRequest -Uri "http://localhost:8080/api/quotes" `
-Method POST `
-ContentType "application/json" `
-Body '{"productId": 1, "zoneCode": "TUN", "clientName": "Jane", "clientAge": 20}'
4. 📄 Get All Quotes

Fetch all stored quotes.

Request
Invoke-WebRequest -Uri "http://localhost:8080/api/quotes" -Method GET
5. 🔎 Filter by Product ID

Fetch quotes filtered by product ID.

Request
Invoke-WebRequest -Uri "http://localhost:8080/api/quotes?productId=1" -Method GET
6. 💰 Filter by Minimum Price

Fetch quotes where price is above a minimum value.

Request
Invoke-WebRequest -Uri "http://localhost:8080/api/quotes?minPrice=600" -Method GET
7. ❌ Test 404 (Non-existent Quote)

Used to test error handling when quote does not exist.

Request
Invoke-WebRequest -Uri "http://localhost:8080/api/quotes/999" -Method GET